The **15-0add-9deg-250s-N2-1600s** condition is the most promising Pareto candidate combining high pore fraction (0.77–0.85) with moderate-to-good modulus (~247–277 bar). Run1 was clean; run5 had a top gap but showed 0.85 pore fraction. Runs 2–9 show high variability in both objectives and membrane quality. This condition has 9 runs but with substantial scatter (pore fraction 0.50–0.85, modulus 198–315 bar, CV often high), and membrane quality is inconsistent. The condition is not yet reproducibly confirmed as a Pareto improvement.

**Validation status:** The 15wt%/9°C/250s/N2/1600s condition has multiple runs but no clean pair of independent repeats both showing high pore fraction AND high modulus simultaneously. Run1 (clean, 0.77 PF, 247 modulus) and run8 (clean, 0.68 PF, 211 modulus) are the two cleanest specimens — they show meaningful scatter. Run5 (0.85 PF, 277 modulus) had a top-gap defect. The condition warrants one more clean independent repeat to confirm whether the high-PF/moderate-modulus performance is reproducible.

**Alternative consideration:** The 14p5-0add-10deg-200s-N2-1500s condition (runs 1–4) shows consistently good pore fraction (0.65–0.69) with modulus 209–270 bar and mostly clean membranes — a reliable mid-Pareto candidate already reasonably validated.

**Decision:** Validate 15wt%/9°C bath/250s wait/N2/1600s with one more independent synthesis. This is the highest-pore-fraction candidate on the Pareto front with meaningful modulus, but its performance is not yet reproducibly confirmed across clean specimens. The large run-to-run scatter (PF SD across runs ~0.10+, modulus range ~100 bar) and inconsistent membrane quality mean we cannot treat it as confirmed. One more clean repeat will clarify whether the (0.77, 247) or (0.85, 277) level is achievable reproducibly.

